#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><bridgehead>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:98
#, xml-text
msgid "Linux PAM Dependencies"
msgstr "Dependências do Linux PAM"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><bridgehead>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:100
#, xml-text
msgid "Optional"
msgstr "Opcionais"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:102
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"libnsl\"/>, <xref linkend=\"libtirpc\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"rpcsvc-proto\"/>, &berkeley-db;, <ulink "
"url=\"https://github.com/linux-audit/audit-userspace\">libaudit</ulink>, "
"<ulink url=\"https://github.com/openSUSE/libeconf\">libeconf</ulink>, and "
"<ulink url=\"https://www.prelude-siem.org\">Prelude</ulink>"
msgstr ""
"<xref linkend=\"libnsl\"/>, <xref linkend=\"libtirpc\"/>, <xref linkend"
"=\"rpcsvc-proto\"/>, &berkeley-db;, <ulink url=\"https://github.com/"
"linux-audit/audit-userspace\">libaudit</ulink>, <ulink url=\"https://github."
"com/openSUSE/libeconf\">libeconf</ulink> e <ulink url=\"https://www.prelude-"
"siem.org\">Prelude</ulink>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:125
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"shadow\"/> <phrase revision=\"systemd\"> "
"and <xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"systemd\"/> must</phrase><phrase "
"revision=\"sysv\">must</phrase> be reinstalled and reconfigured after "
"installing and configuring <application>Linux PAM</application>."
msgstr ""
"<xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"shadow\"/> <phrase revision=\"systemd\"> e "
"<xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"systemd\"/> precisa</phrase><phrase "
"revision=\"sysv\">precisa</phrase> ser reinstalado e reconfigurado depois de"
" instalar e de configurar o <application>Linux PAM</application>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:133
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"With Linux-PAM-1.4.0 and higher, the pam_cracklib module is not installed by"
" default. Use <xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"libpwquality\"/> to enforce "
"strong passwords."
msgstr ""
"Com o Linux-PAM-1.4.0 e superior, o módulo pam_cracklib não é instalado por "
"padrão. Use <xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"libpwquality\"/> para impor "
"senhas fortes."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:142
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Linux PAM"
msgstr "Instalação do Linux PAM"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:145
#, xml-text
msgid "First, prevent the installation of an unneeded systemd file:"
msgstr "Primeiro, evite a instalação de um arquivo desnecessário do systemd:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:148
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sed -e /service_DATA/d \\\n"
"    -i modules/pam_namespace/Makefile.am &amp;&amp;\n"
"autoreconf</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>sed -e /service_DATA/d \\\n"
"   -i modules/pam_namespace/Makefile.am &amp;&amp;\n"
"autoreconf</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:153
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you downloaded the documentation, unpack the tarball by issuing the "
"following command."
msgstr ""
"Se você baixou a documentação, [então] desempacote o tarball emitindo o "
"seguinte comando."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:157
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>tar -xf ../Linux-PAM-&linux-pam-docs-version;-docs.tar.xz "
"--strip-components=1</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>tar -xf ../Linux-PAM-&linux-pam-docs-version;-docs.tar.xz "
"--strip-components=1</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:169
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Compile and link <application>Linux PAM</application> by running the "
"following commands:"
msgstr ""
"Compile e vincule o <application>Linux PAM</application> executando os "
"seguintes comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:173
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>./configure --prefix=/usr                        \\\n"
"            --sbindir=/usr/sbin                  \\\n"
"            --sysconfdir=/etc                    \\\n"
"            --libdir=/usr/lib                    \\\n"
"            --enable-securedir=/usr/lib/security \\\n"
"            --docdir=/usr/share/doc/Linux-PAM-&linux-pam-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>./configure --prefix=/usr                       \\\n"
"            --sbindir=/usr/sbin                  \\\n"
"            --sysconfdir=/etc                    \\\n"
"            --libdir=/usr/lib                    \\\n"
"            --enable-securedir=/usr/lib/security \\\n"
"            --docdir=/usr/share/doc/Linux-PAM-&linux-pam-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:182
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test the results, a suitable <filename>/etc/pam.d/other</filename> "
"configuration file must exist."
msgstr ""
"Para testar os resultados, um arquivo de configuração adequado "
"<filename>/etc/pam.d/other</filename> precisa existir."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><caution><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:187
#, xml-text
msgid "Reinstallation or Upgrade of Linux PAM"
msgstr "Reinstalação ou Atualização do Linux PAM"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><caution><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:189
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you have a system with Linux PAM installed and working, be careful when "
"modifying the files in <filename class=\"directory\">/etc/pam.d</filename>, "
"since your system may become totally unusable. If you want to run the tests,"
" you do not need to create another <filename>/etc/pam.d/other</filename> "
"file. The existing file can be used for the tests."
msgstr ""
"Se você tiver um sistema com Linux PAM instalado e funcionando, seja "
"cuidadoso(a) ao modificar os arquivos em <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc/pam.d</filename>, pois seu sistema possivelmente se"
" torne totalmente inutilizável. Se você deseja executar os testes, [então] "
"não precisa criar outro arquivo <filename>/etc/pam.d/other</filename>. O "
"arquivo existente pode ser usado para os testes."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><caution><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:198
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You should also be aware that <command>make install</command> overwrites the"
" configuration files in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc/security</filename> as well as "
"<filename>/etc/environment</filename>. If you have modified those files, be "
"sure to back them up."
msgstr ""
"Você também deveria estar ciente de que <command>make install</command> "
"sobrescreve os arquivos de configuração em <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc/security</filename>, assim como em "
"<filename>/etc/environment</filename> . Se você tiver modificado esses "
"arquivos, [então] certifique-se de produzir uma cópia de segurança deles."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:207
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For a first-time installation, create a configuration file by issuing the "
"following commands as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> "
"user:"
msgstr ""
"Para uma primeira instalação, crie um arquivo de configuração emitindo os "
"seguintes comandos como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:212
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>install -v -m755 -d /etc/pam.d &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/other &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>auth     required       pam_deny.so\n"
"account  required       pam_deny.so\n"
"password required       pam_deny.so\n"
"session  required       pam_deny.so</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>install -v -m755 -d /etc/pam.d &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/other &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>auth     required       pam_deny.so\n"
"account  required       pam_deny.so\n"
"password required      pam_deny.so\n"
"session  required       pam_deny.so</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:222
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now run the tests by issuing <command>make check</command>.  Be sure the "
"tests produced no errors before continuing the installation. Note that the "
"tests are very long.  Redirect the output to a log file, so you can inspect "
"it thoroughly."
msgstr ""
"Agora execute os testes emitindo <command>make check</command>. Certifique-"
"se de que os testes não produziram erros antes de continuar a instalação. "
"Observe que os testes são muito longos. Redirecione a saída gerada para um "
"arquivo de registro, de forma que você possa inspecioná-lo completamente."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:229
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For a first-time installation, remove the configuration file created earlier"
" by issuing the following command as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Para uma primeira instalação, remova o arquivo de configuração criado "
"anteriormente emitindo o seguinte comando como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:234
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>rm -fv /etc/pam.d/other</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>rm -fv /etc/pam.d/other</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:237
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Agora, como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:241
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>make install &amp;&amp;\n"
"chmod -v 4755 /usr/sbin/unix_chkpwd</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>make install &amp;&amp;\n"
"chmod -v 4755 /usr/sbin/unix_chkpwd</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:247
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr "Explicações do Comando"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:250
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--enable-securedir=/usr/lib/security</parameter>: This switch "
"sets the installation location for the <application>PAM</application> "
"modules."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--enable-securedir=/usr/lib/security</parameter>: Essa chave "
"configura o local de instalação para os módulos "
"<application>PAM</application>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:267
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>chmod -v 4755 /usr/sbin/unix_chkpwd</command>: The setuid bit for "
"the <command>unix_chkpwd</command> helper program must be turned on, so that"
" non-<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> processes can access "
"the shadow file."
msgstr ""
"<command>chmod -v 4755 /usr/sbin/unix_chkpwd</command>: O bit setuid para o "
"aplicativo auxiliar <command>unix_chkpwd</command> precisa ser ativado, de "
"forma que processos não <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> "
"possam acessar o arquivo de sombra."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:276
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring Linux-PAM"
msgstr "Configurando Linux-PAM"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:279
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuration Files"
msgstr "Arquivos de Configuração"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:282
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<filename>/etc/security/*</filename> and <filename>/etc/pam.d/*</filename>"
msgstr ""
"<filename>/etc/security/*</filename> e <filename>/etc/pam.d/*</filename>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:287
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/security/*"
msgstr "/etc/security/*"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:291
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/pam.d/*"
msgstr "/etc/pam.d/*"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:297
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuration Information"
msgstr "Informação de Configuração"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:300
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Configuration information is placed in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc/pam.d/</filename>.  Here is a sample file:"
msgstr ""
"A informação de configuração é colocada em <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/etc/pam.d/</filename>. Aqui está um arquivo de amostra:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:305
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/other\n"
"\n"
"auth            required        pam_unix.so     nullok\n"
"account         required        pam_unix.so\n"
"session         required        pam_unix.so\n"
"password        required        pam_unix.so     nullok\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/other</literal>"
msgstr ""
"<literal># Início /etc/pam.d/other\n"
"\n"
"auth            required        pam_unix.so     nullok\n"
"account         required        pam_unix.so\n"
"session         required        pam_unix.so\n"
"password        required        pam_unix.so     nullok\n"
"\n"
"# Fim /etc/pam.d/other</literal>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:315
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now create some generic configuration files.  As the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Agora, crie alguns arquivos genéricos de configuração. Como o(a) usuário(a) "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:319
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>install -vdm755 /etc/pam.d &amp;&amp;\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-account &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/system-account\n"
"\n"
"account   required    pam_unix.so\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/system-account</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-auth &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/system-auth\n"
"\n"
"auth      required    pam_unix.so\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/system-auth</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-session &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/system-session\n"
"\n"
"session   required    pam_unix.so\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/system-session</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-password &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/system-password\n"
"\n"
"# use yescrypt hash for encryption, use shadow, and try to use any\n"
"# previously defined authentication token (chosen password) set by any\n"
"# prior module.\n"
"password  required    pam_unix.so       yescrypt shadow try_first_pass\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/system-password</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>install -vdm755 /etc/pam.d &amp;&amp;\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-account &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/pam.d/system-account\n"
"\n"
"account   required    pam_unix.so\n"
"\n"
"# Termina /etc/pam.d/system-account</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-auth &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/pam.d/system-auth\n"
"\n"
"auth      required    pam_unix.so\n"
"\n"
"# Termina /etc/pam.d/system-auth</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-session &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/pam.d/system-session\n"
"\n"
"session   required    pam_unix.so\n"
"\n"
"# Termina /etc/pam.d/system-session</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-password &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/pam.d/system-password\n"
"\n"
"# Use resumo 'yescrypt' para encriptação; use sombra e tente usar\n"
"# qualquer token de autenticação previamente definido (senha escolhida)\n"
"# configurado por qualquer módulo anterior.\n"
"password  required    pam_unix.so       yescrypt shadow try_first_pass\n"
"\n"
"# Termina /etc/pam.d/system-password</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:357
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you wish to enable strong password support, install <xref "
"linkend=\"libpwquality\"/>, and follow the instructions on that page to "
"configure the pam_pwquality PAM module with strong password support."
msgstr ""
"Se você deseja ativar o suporte a senhas fortes, [então] instale <xref "
"linkend=\"libpwquality\"/> e siga as instruções naquela página para "
"configurar o módulo PAM pam_pwquality com suporte a senhas fortes."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:364
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Next, add a restrictive <filename>/etc/pam.d/other</filename> configuration "
"file.  With this file, programs that are PAM aware will not run unless a "
"configuration file specifically for that application exists."
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, adicione um arquivo de configuração "
"<filename>/etc/pam.d/other</filename> restritivo. Com esse arquivo, os "
"aplicativos que reconhecem o PAM não serão executados, a menos que exista um"
" arquivo de configuração específico para esse aplicativo."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/security/linux-pam.xml:370
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/other &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/other\n"
"\n"
"auth        required        pam_warn.so\n"
"auth        required        pam_deny.so\n"
"account     required        pam_warn.so\n"
"account     required        pam_deny.so\n"
"password    required        pam_warn.so\n"
"password    required        pam_deny.so\n"
"session     required        pam_warn.so\n"
"session     required        pam_deny.so\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/other</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/other &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Início /etc/pam.d/other\n"
"\n"
"auth        required        pam_warn.so\n"
"auth        required        pam_deny.so\n"
"account     required        pam_warn.so\n"
"account     required        pam_deny.so\n"
"password    required        pam_warn.so\n"
"password    required        pam_deny.so\n"
"session     required        pam_warn.so\n"
"session     required        pam_deny.so\n"
"\n"
"# Fim /etc/pam.d/other</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

